Lab 1: Create a GitHub Repository

Objective: Learn source control basics.

Tasks:

Create a GitHub repository.
Clone it locally.
Create a README.md.
Commit and push the changes.
Create a feature branch.
Merge it using a Pull Request.

Skills: Git, branching, PR workflow.

Lab 2: Install Azure CLI

Tasks:

az login
az account show
az group list

Skills: Azure CLI basics.

Lab 3: Install Docker

Tasks:

docker --version
docker run hello-world
docker ps
docker images

Skills: Docker installation and verification.

Lab 4: Install kubectl

Tasks:

kubectl version --client
kubectl config view

Skills: Kubernetes CLI basics.

Lab 5: Build Your First CI Pipeline

Create a simple GitHub Actions workflow:

name: First CI

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Print Message
        run: echo "Hello Azure DevOps"

Push it to GitHub and verify the workflow succeeds.

Skills: CI fundamentals.

Lab 6: Introduce a Build Failure

Modify the workflow:

- name: Fail Build
  run: exit 1

Observe:

Pipeline failure
Logs
Error messages

Skills: Troubleshooting pipelines.

Lab 7: Add a Manual Approval Environment

In GitHub:

Create an environment named Production.
Configure required reviewers.
Update the workflow to deploy to that environment.

This demonstrates Continuous Delivery.

